# E429 draft — Conan OpenSSL ABI alignment for reused binaries

id:                     E1462
trigger_tool:           conan|ld|runtime
phase:                  dependency-resolve|linking|runtime
error_signature:        Version conflict.*openssl|libnice/0[.]1[.]21.*OpenSSL 1[.]1[.]1w.*libwebsockets/4[.]3[.]5[.]1.*OpenSSL 3[.]5[.]6
severity:               2
category:               linking, conan, dependency, runtime
match_keywords:          Conan, OpenSSL ABI, prebuilt binary, libnice, libwebsockets, version override
title:                  Align OpenSSL ABI across reused Conan binaries and source-built dependencies
root_cause:              A Conan version override changes the selected dependency graph but does not rebuild a previously published binary. Reusing a libnice binary built against OpenSSL 1.1.1w while compiling libwebsockets against its default OpenSSL 3.5.6 can leave components in one process with incompatible OpenSSL ABI assumptions.
affected_scope:          Conan application graphs that combine a reused binary package with a source-built TLS dependency whose OpenSSL requirement differs; measured on Janus 1.4.1 for HarmonyOS PC.
verification_cmd:        In the Janus package directory, run the recorded OHOS AArch64 conan create command and confirm the resolved graph selects openssl/1.1.1w; then run the native test_package REST and WebSocket flows on the target.
rec_priority:            1
rec_approach:            align-openssl-to-reused-binary-abi
rec_description:         Read the reused artifact's build-time OpenSSL requirement, pin the consumer graph to that exact version with a root override, and build any incompatible source dependency against the pinned version. Verify the resolved graph and exercise the final executable on the target.
rec_command:             self.requires("openssl/1.1.1w", override=True)  # match the published libnice binary; build libwebsockets from source
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:                conan-recipe
fallback_priority:       2
fallback_approach:       rebuild-binary-dependency-closure
fallback_description:    If a newer OpenSSL is required, rebuild the binary dependency and every affected consumer in one consistent graph; do not treat an override as a binary rebuild.
fallback_command:        conan create <package>/<version> --build=missing
fallback_auto_fix:       false
fallback_impl:           manual
forbid_1_pattern:        override.*openssl/3[.]|libnice/0[.]1[.]21.*openssl/1[.]1[.]1w.*libwebsockets/4[.]3[.]5[.]1.*openssl/3[.]
forbid_1_reason:         A root override only changes Conan graph resolution; it cannot change the OpenSSL ABI already compiled into a reused libnice binary.
forbid_1_consequence:    The graph may appear resolved while Janus links or loads components built against different OpenSSL ABI baselines.
forbid_2_pattern:
forbid_2_reason:
forbid_2_consequence:
principles:
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E429-draft-2C1E.md
last_updated:           2026-10-13
source_event:            Janus 1.4.1 OHOS AArch64 dependency review: published libnice/0.1.21 declares OpenSSL 1.1.1w while libwebsockets/4.3.5.1 defaults to OpenSSL 3.5.6; the graph was aligned before final build, and target REST/WebSocket tests passed.
authors:
source_pr:
source_commit:
metrics_success_count:  0
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     0.0
metrics_last_used:
authors:               2C1E
